Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:45:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Viewer info bar, curve colours and dope sheet keys
 optionally drawn like Nuke's

- viewerInfoCompact (Appearance > Main Window; off by default, Natron's info bar as before): the viewer's info bar
  reads "bbox:" instead of "RoD:", "channels: rgba" (instead of "Color.RGBA32f") after the bbox instead of first,
  the values in brighter red, green and blue with a white alpha, and "H: 51 S:0.05 V:0.86  L: 0.84822". The
  channels move each time an image arrives, so the preference applies without a restart.
- animationEditorsNuke (Appearance > Curve Editor; off by default): the r, g, b and a curves red, green, blue and
  white in the curve editor (other curves keep Natron's colours), and the dope sheet's keys as narrow grey bars with
  a dark edge (the selection colour when selected) instead of the interpolation pictures.
- Every new preference is read by name, so Settings.h doesn't change.

Since the audit of 11 November 2026 (NAT-17): the info bar's preference is named viewerInfoCompact (was
viewerInfoNuke).

Core patch 0007 of the BeeeFX fork (layer/patches/).

Gap: layer/GAPS.md, "Nuke's look and habits" (the info bar, the curve editor and dope sheet).
Size: 4 files, 112 lines added, 18 removed.
upstream: not offered yet (the repository is public since 2 November 2026; offered once the two
fixes are in, Baptiste's call).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
